{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#982","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#982","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#982\",\"parent_revision\":\"2e1d244db95927936b41d039601bd849c1b40a24062638f1b4e06da3e177a64f\",\"root_revision\":\"2e1d244db95927936b41d039601bd849c1b40a24062638f1b4e06da3e177a64f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAs the development harness adds per-project agent/skill preferences, project management backend configuration (GitHub/GitLab/Linear/Supabase credentials), and task-level settings, there is no place to store project-specific preferences or secrets outside the repo. A user-scoped ~/.dh/ directory is needed with: ~/.dh/settings.json for global settings, ~/.dh/secrets.json (or equivalent) for credentials, and ~/.dh/projects/{project-path-as-slug}/ for per-project preferences that load automatically without being committed to the repo. Design needs research \u2014 Charmbracelet Crush (https://github.com/charmbracelet/crush) is the reference system to study for config, secrets, and project settings patterns. Research first: How does Crush handle config vs secrets separation, project-scoped overrides, and credential storage?\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | Charmbracelet Crush config patterns (research prerequisite) | MISSING | Must be researched first per item description |\\n| 2 | `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/` already used by backlog state | AVAILABLE | CLAUDE.md DH state location documentation |\\n| 3 | Existing settings that would move to config (GITHUB_TOKEN, etc.) | AVAILABLE | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github.py` |\\n| 4 | Config format decision (JSON, TOML, YAML) | MISSING | Depends on Crush research findings |\\n| 5 | Secret storage security model (keychain vs encrypted file vs plain 0600) | MISSING | Architecture decision required |\\n\\nVerdict: BLOCKED \u2014 Crush research must complete first. Recommend spawning `@dh:ecosystem-researcher` with Crush URL from item description.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP1 Feature. High complexity. Security-sensitive (secrets handling). Requires architecture research before implementation.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- `~/.dh/settings.json` stores global settings (format TBD after Crush research)\\n- `~/.dh/secrets.json` (or equivalent) stores credentials with appropriate file permissions (0600)\\n- `~/.dh/projects/{project-path-as-slug}/` stores per-project preferences that load automatically when dh is used in that project\\n- Config is loaded in priority order: project-specific overrides global\\n- At least one existing dh setting (e.g., GitHub token, backend URL) migrated to use the new config system\\n- Charmbracelet Crush patterns researched: how Crush handles config/secrets separation, project-scoped overrides, and credential storage\\n- Backward compat: existing hardcoded env vars continue to work; config system is additive\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `~/.dh/settings.json` \u2014 new global settings file (created at runtime)\\n- `~/.dh/secrets.json` \u2014 new credentials file (created at runtime, 0600)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/config.py` \u2014 new config loader module\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github.py` \u2014 update to use config loader\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a developer using the development harness on multiple machines and projects, I need a `~/.dh/` user-scoped config system with project settings and secrets management so I can store per-project preferences and credentials outside the repo without committing sensitive data.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **user-scoped ~/.dh/ config system with project settings and secrets management** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: User request \u2014 session 2026-03-21, vision for DH config management as backends and per-project settings grow\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"0c046ead5f8deadd1c692906f35e98618d276e79a40b19f8b7b901081b312f42\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTE9wQ\"}"}